OBSERVATIONS (not grounds for FAIL)
 O1. A `VERDICT: PASS` whose own criteria include `pass:false` is recorded as PASS (verdict/pass flags never cross-checked); a FAIL with empty evidence is recorded (brief
     only guards PASS). `​` counts as non-empty evidence.
 O2. Exclusion is by NAME only: a hard link (or copy) of an excluded file under another name is copied verbatim (fixture: `ln realdata/secret.csv notes-hardlink.txt`
     -> content in /work). `.env*`/`.pem`/`.key` are BASENAME rules per the brief, so files inside a directory named `.env`/`x.pem` are copied; case variants (`.ENV`,
     `Data/`) are not excluded; other credential names (id_rsa, .netrc, credentials.json, *.sqlite) rely on codex.exclude.
 O3. codex.exclude semantics per brief but footguns: `private` (no slash) does not exclude `private/*`; `private/` matches only at the tree root (`x/private/n.txt`
     copied); `./private/` matches nothing; a UTF-8 BOM defeats the first line.
 O4. classify/6b scan every STRING value of error/turn.failed events, not only the message: `{"type":"error","message":"boom","thread_id":"019a4290-.."}` -> quota
     (429 inside an id). Integer status fields are ignored.
 O5. ORACLE BLIND SPOT: the suffix-lookalike probe `chatgpt.com.evil.invalid` cannot see a proxy filter missing the `$` anchor. Experiment: mutant filter `^chatgpt\.com`
     (no `$`) -> `curl --proxy` to https://chatgpt.com.evil.invalid/ gives code=000 rc=56, identical to the correct proxy (the mutant's log shows
     `opensock: opening connection to chatgpt.com.evil.invalid:443`, then NXDOMAIN). The shipped filter IS anchored (`api.openai.com.evil.com:443` -> 403 Filtered).
     A resolvable lookalike or an assertion on proxy.log would close it.
 O6. Oracle "P no host path visible" checks a hard-coded path list; the real mount set is only proven by my mountinfo read (clean).
 O7. Proxy: plain-HTTP requests to the three allowlisted hosts on ANY port are forwarded (`GET http://chatgpt.com:<p>/` opens a connection to chatgpt.com:<p>); only CONNECT is
     port-restricted (brief-conformant). `CONNECT chatgpt.com:0443` / `:+443` accepted (still 443).
 O8. Container /etc/resolv.conf carries the host's DNS search domain (`otter-lungfish.ts.net`, the tailnet name); mountinfo exposes host path strings of the mount sources.
 O9. No lock for two concurrent invocations at the same (T,A) (they share $AUD/out); parent-directory symlink checks are made at listing time only (final component uses
     O_NOFOLLOW) -- exploitable only by a concurrent local writer to the tree.
 O10. The `ln` "appeared meanwhile" branch still prints "wrote <verdict>" before exiting (cosmetic).
